## Differences (every one)

1. `shots.json` `duration_s`: published 150.04, rebuild 150.108345. Cause: ffprobe reports the video stream as 150.041667 s and the audio stream as 150.108345 s; crewcut's `shots._probe` reads the container `format.duration` (the longer one), the published value matches the video stream (rounded to 2 decimals). It is the only byte difference of the three annotation files; `hierarchy.json` carries 150.04 in both. No cut, task id or task field depends on it. Which duration is intended is not stated in the documents: open item O4 for the maintainer, not decided here.
2. Task descriptions: empty in the rebuild (VLM not run, no key, D5). The published dataset's task list has no description field, so nothing to compare; no conclusion drawn.
3. Not comparable: the published dataset has no provenance index, no task input files and no truth.json for this film; the rebuilt `provenance.npz` (no DINOv2) is not compared with anything.
4. ASR backend: published draft came from whisper.cpp, rebuild used faster-whisper (D3); both give zero lines here.

The Issue #3 s1.6 defects reproduced: the largest-file master choice (record/raw/annotate_attempt1_largest_file.log) and the PeerTube 'Attribution' label rejected by `audit.decide` (O1, O2). The first was worked around by decision D2; the licence one by D1.

5. Key `cuts` at segment end (raised by scorer, issue #8): in 32 of 90 key files the last cut equals the segment duration (e.g. caminandes3-L1-0000: cuts [21.375, 30.5, 32.292], duration 32.292). Cause: `segment_truth` filters `a < c < b` on the unrounded cut time (32.29167) against the rounded segment end (32.292). The published dataset has no truth.json, so it cannot be compared; the rebuild equals it on everything it publishes. Left as produced; open item O5 for the maintainer.
